112
00:07:33,361 --> 00:07:38,360
When a latent fingerprint is found at the scene of a crime,

113
00:07:38,361 --> 00:07:44,360
it can be lifted, imaged, searched against a database

114
00:07:44,361 --> 00:07:47,860
of millions of individuals, and with a matter of minutes,

115
00:07:47,861 --> 00:07:49,860
identify an individual.

116
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:55,500
New imaging techniques allow modern investigators

117
00:07:55,501 --> 00:07:58,100
to detect previously invisible prints.

118
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:01,380
It used to be at a crime scene.

119
00:08:01,381 --> 00:08:03,980
They'd turn on all the lights as brightly as they could.

120
00:08:03,981 --> 00:08:06,040
It was they would shed some light on the crime.

121
00:08:06,041 --> 00:08:08,360
Now what they do is they turn out the lights,

122
00:08:08,361 --> 00:08:11,980
and they put on infrared detectors, heat detectors.

123
00:08:11,981 --> 00:08:14,020
They use all kinds of different devices

124
00:08:14,021 --> 00:08:16,520
to find things that can't be seen by the naked eye,

125
00:08:16,521 --> 00:08:19,020
but which may very well be good lead evidence.

126
00:08:19,021 --> 00:08:23,020
New technologies can solve old mysteries.

127
00:08:23,021 --> 00:08:30,020
In 1982, Valerian Trefa, Romanian Orthodox Bishop of Cleveland,

128
00:08:30,021 --> 00:08:34,020
